   "text": "I read the molecule in sections and wrote each one as SMILES, then joined them.\n\n**Left end.** An indazole carries a 3-carbon chain on N1. The chain ends in an NH attached to C2 of a 1,4,5,6-tetrahydropyrimidine ring. The indazole C5 bears a carbonyl that forms an amide with the NH\u2013CH2 of the next unit.\n\n**Diaminopropionate unit.** The amide NH\u2013CH2 leads to a stereocentre carrying a methyl ester (C(=O)OMe) and an NH\u2013SO2 group. The wedge points to the ester carbon with H at the back, which gives the S configuration.\n\n**Centre.** The sulfonamide sits on one para position of a biphenyl, and a second SO2\u2013NH sits on the other para position. That NH continues through \u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013 to a C(=O).\n\n**Glutamate unit (right end).** The C(=O) is attached to the glutamate \u03b1-carbon, which carries an NH\u2013Cbz group (C(=O)OCH2Ph) and a side chain CH2CH2C(=O)O-tBu. The wedge points to the side-chain CH2 with H at the back, which gives the S configuration.\n\nI checked the chirality tags by working out the neighbour order at each stereocentre against the CIP priorities. They come out S for both centres, matching the drawing.\n\nSMILES: O=C(c1ccc2c(cnn2CCCNC2=NCCCN2)c1)NC[C@H](NS(=O)(=O)c1ccc(cc1)-c1ccc(cc1)S(=O)(=O)NCCNC(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)OCc1ccccc1)CCC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)C(=O)OC"
